v4.2.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Contoso Industrial Global Warranty Policy  \\\\r\\\\n_Version 4.2 \\\\u2014 effective 2025-04-01_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nPOL-WAR-4.2\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Version**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n4.2\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Effective from**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n2025-04-01\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Document owner**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nWarranty Operations\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Applies to**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nAll products, all regions, all authorised service partners\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Supersedes**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nPOL-WAR-4.1 (effective 1 April 2024)\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Purpose\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis policy sets out the warranty Contoso Industrial provides on equipment it manufactures, the basis on which a claim from an authorised service partner is adjudicated, and the amounts payable. It applies to every claim submitted through the service claim system.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 1. Interpretation\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 1.4  Precedence between instruments\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nWhere two or more instruments address the same asset, the order of precedence is: (a) a Technical Service Bulletin that names the serial range of the asset; (b) the Regional Addendum for the region in which the asset is installed; (c) this policy. A Bulletin that has been superseded has no effect, whether or not it remains published. Where the Bulletin document and the service system applicability index disagree, the Bulletin document governs; the index is maintained for reporting and is informational only.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 2. Coverage\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 2.1  Standard coverage period\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nUnless extended or varied by an instrument of higher precedence, an asset is covered for twenty-four (24) months from the date of commissioning, or six thousand (6,000) running hours, whichever occurs first.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 2.3  Assets with no commissioning record\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nWhere the commissioning record for an asset is absent from the asset registry, coverage cannot be determined. The claim is to be held and the commissioning certificate requested from the installing partner. The date of despatch or the date of installation must not be substituted for the date of commissioning.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 4. Amounts payable\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 4.1  Labour\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nLabour is payable at the flat-rate allowance published for the operation code in the current Flat Rate Labour schedule, or at the hours actually claimed, whichever is the lesser. The rate applied is the regional labour rate in force on the date of repair.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 4.2  Parts\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nParts are payable at the published list price for the region, for the part actually fitted. Where a part has been superseded, the price of the superseding part applies.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 4.3  Handling\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nA handling uplift on parts is payable only where the partner\\\\u0027s Service Partner Agreement expressly grants one, at the percentage stated in that agreement.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 5. Exclusions\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 5.1  Exclusion - misuse and overload\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nDamage arising from operation outside the published duty envelope, including sustained overload, is excluded.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 5.2  Exclusion - fluid contamination\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nDamage arising from hydraulic fluid contamination above ISO 4406 class 18/16/13 is excluded, save where a Technical Service Bulletin provides otherwise.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 5.3  Exclusion - unauthorised modification\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nDamage arising from modification not authorised in writing by Contoso Industrial is excluded.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 5.4  Exclusion - consumables\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nFilters, fluids, belts, seals and other consumables are excluded when replaced as scheduled maintenance. Scheduled maintenance is not claimable under warranty and has no warranty operation code, so a consumable claimed under a warranty repair operation code is treated as a corrective repair and is covered, unless an inspection report records the replacement as routine.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 6. Repair warranty\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 6.1  Repair warranty\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nA component replaced under warranty carries a further ninety (90) days of coverage from the date the repair was completed. A claim arising within that period is adjudicated under this clause and carries funding code RW, whether or not the underlying asset remains within its coverage period.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 7. Goodwill and authority\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 7.1  Goodwill authority\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nAn amount payable outside coverage may be authorised as goodwill only by a person holding the tier of authority set out in the Goodwill and Authority Matrix for that amount, and only where the authority is recorded in the claim system. An approval given in conversation, in a channel message, or by telephone does not constitute authority for the purposes of this clause.\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.8735347},{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\r\\\\n## Annexes\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThe Flat Rate Labour schedule, the regional labour rate schedule and the parts price list are maintained separately and published in the Warranty Operations library. The Goodwill and Authority Matrix referred to at clause 7.1 is published alongside this policy.\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.7248977}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/03-RateCards/Flat-Rate-Labour-FY26.xlsx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022Flat-Rate-Labour-FY26\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022openpyxl;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022Flat-Rate-Labour-FY26.xlsx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/03-RateCards/Flat-Rate-Labour-FY26.xlsx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\u003Csheet_1\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Flat Rate Labour\\\\r\\\\nFlat Rate Labour Schedule \\\\u2014 FY26\\\\r\\\\nContoso Industrial \\\\u00B7 Warranty Operations \\\\u00B7 effective 1 April 2026 \\\\u00B7 hours payable per operation, per policy clause 4.1\\\\r\\\\nOperation code\\\\r\\\\nDescription\\\\r\\\\nProduct family\\\\r\\\\nComponent\\\\r\\\\nFlat-rate hours\\\\r\\\\nHYD-PUMP-RR\\\\r\\\\nHydraulic pump - remove and replace\\\\r\\\\n4000-series industrial chiller\\\\r\\\\nhydraulic\\\\r\\\\n5.5\\\\r\\\\nFILT-HSG-RR\\\\r\\\\nFilter housing - remove and replace\\\\r\\\\n4000-series industrial chiller\\\\r\\\\nhydraulic\\\\r\\\\n2.5\\\\r\\\\nCOMP-RR\\\\r\\\\nCompressor module - remove and replace\\\\r\\\\n4000-series industrial chiller\\\\r\\\\ncompressor\\\\r\\\\n9\\\\r\\\\nCTRL-BD-RR\\\\r\\\\nControl board - replace\\\\r\\\\n4000-series industrial chiller\\\\r\\\\ncontrols\\\\r\\\\n1.5\\\\r\\\\nCOND-FAN-RR\\\\r\\\\nCondenser fan assembly - replace\\\\r\\\\n4000-series industrial chiller\\\\r\\\\nstructure\\\\r\\\\n3.5\\\\r\\\\nVALVE-PLT-RR\\\\r\\\\nValve plate kit - replace\\\\r\\\\n2200-series air compressor\\\\r\\\\nvalve plate\\\\r\\\\n4\\\\r\\\\nMOTOR-RR\\\\r\\\\nDrive motor - replace\\\\r\\\\n2200-series air compressor\\\\r\\\\ndrive\\\\r\\\\n7.5\\\\r\\\\nBEARING-RR\\\\r\\\\nMain bearing set - replace\\\\r\\\\n2200-series air compressor\\\\r\\\\ndrive\\\\r\\\\n6\\\\r\\\\nSEAL-KIT-RR\\\\r\\\\nSeal kit - replace\\\\r\\\\n2200-series air compressor\\\\r\\\\nseals\\\\r\\\\n3\\\\r\\\\nDIAG-FIELD\\\\r\\\\nField diagnostic visit\\\\r\\\\nany\\\\r\\\\nany\\\\r\\\\n2\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/sheet_1\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Csheet_2\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Notes\\\\r\\\\nFlat Rate Labour Schedule \\\\u2014 FY26\\\\r\\\\nLabour is payable at the flat-rate allowance for the operation code, or at the\\\\r\\\\nhours actually claimed, whichever is the lesser (Global Warranty Policy, 4.1).\\\\r\\\\nHours above the flat-rate allowance are not payable and are reported to the\\\\r\\\\npartner as a variance on the adjudication.\\\\r\\\\nThe rate applied to these hours is the regional labour rate in force on the\\\\r\\\\ndate of repair. See Labour-Rates-By-Region-FY26.xlsx.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/sheet_2\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.72701746}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/01-Policy/ADD-IN-2.1 Regional Addendum - India v2.1.docx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022ADD-IN-2.1 Regional Addendum - India v2.1\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022python-docx;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022ADD-IN-2.1 Regional Addendum - India v2.1.docx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/01-Policy/ADD-IN-2.1 Regional Addendum - India v2.1.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Regional Addendum - India  \\\\r\\\\n_Version 2.1 \\\\u2014 effective 2025-04-01_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nADD-IN-2.1\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Region**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nIndia\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Currency**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nINR\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Effective from**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n2025-04-01\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Read with**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nPOL-WAR-4.2 Contoso Industrial Global Warranty Policy\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Scope\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis addendum varies the Global Warranty Policy for equipment installed in India. Where this addendum is silent, the Global Warranty Policy applies without variation. Where a Technical Service Bulletin names the serial range of an asset, clause 1.4 of the Global Warranty Policy governs the order of precedence.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### A1  Varied coverage period\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nFor assets installed in India, the standard coverage period at clause 2.1 of the Global Warranty Policy is varied to eighteen (18) months from the date of commissioning, or five thousand (5,000) running hours, whichever occurs first.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### A3  Coastal and monsoon exclusion\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nCorrosion damage at a coastal installation arising between 1 June and 30 September is excluded, save where a Technical Service Bulletin provides otherwise.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Summary of varied terms\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Term**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Global policy**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**India**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nCoverage period\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 months\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n18 months\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nRunning-hours limit\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n5,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.812503}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/01-Policy/ADD-AP-1.1 Regional Addendum - APAC v1.1.docx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022ADD-AP-1.1 Regional Addendum - APAC v1.1\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022python-docx;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022ADD-AP-1.1 Regional Addendum - APAC v1.1.docx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/01-Policy/ADD-AP-1.1 Regional Addendum - APAC v1.1.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Regional Addendum - APAC  \\\\r\\\\n_Version 1.1 \\\\u2014 effective 2025-04-01_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nADD-AP-1.1\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Region**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nAPAC\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Currency**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nSGD\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Effective from**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n2025-04-01\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Read with**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nPOL-WAR-4.2 Contoso Industrial Global Warranty Policy\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Scope\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis addendum varies the Global Warranty Policy for equipment installed in APAC. Where this addendum is silent, the Global Warranty Policy applies without variation. Where a Technical Service Bulletin names the serial range of an asset, clause 1.4 of the Global Warranty Policy governs the order of precedence.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### A1  Coverage period\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThe standard coverage period at clause 2.1 of the Global Warranty Policy applies without variation.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Summary of varied terms\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Term**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Global policy**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**APAC**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nCoverage period\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 months\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 months\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nRunning-hours limit\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.820755}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/01-Policy/ADD-EM-1.3 Regional Addendum - EMEA v1.3.docx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022ADD-EM-1.3 Regional Addendum - EMEA v1.3\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022python-docx;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022ADD-EM-1.3 Regional Addendum - EMEA v1.3.docx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/01-Policy/ADD-EM-1.3 Regional Addendum - EMEA v1.3.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Regional Addendum - EMEA  \\\\r\\\\n_Version 1.3 \\\\u2014 effective 2024-10-01_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nADD-EM-1.3\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Region**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nEMEA\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Currency**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nEUR\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Effective from**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n2024-10-01\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Read with**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nPOL-WAR-4.2 Contoso Industrial Global Warranty Policy\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Scope\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis addendum varies the Global Warranty Policy for equipment installed in EMEA. Where this addendum is silent, the Global Warranty Policy applies without variation. Where a Technical Service Bulletin names the serial range of an asset, clause 1.4 of the Global Warranty Policy governs the order of precedence.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### A1  Coverage period\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThe standard coverage period at clause 2.1 of the Global Warranty Policy applies without variation.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### A2  Currency\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nAmounts are payable in euro at the published EMEA rates.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Summary of varied terms\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Term**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Global policy**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**EMEA**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nCoverage period\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 months\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 months\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nRunning-hours limit\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.8102744}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/04-PartnerAgreements/SPA-2023-FAB-IN Fabrikam Service Partners.docx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022SPA-2023-FAB-IN Fabrikam Service Partners\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022python-docx;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022SPA-2023-FAB-IN Fabrikam Service Partners.docx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/04-PartnerAgreements/SPA-2023-FAB-IN Fabrikam Service Partners.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Service Partner Agreement  \\\\r\\\\n_Fabrikam Service Partners \\\\u2014 SPA-2023-FAB-IN_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Agreement reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nSPA-2023-FAB-IN\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Partner**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nFabrikam Service Partners\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Partner code**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nD-IN-01\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Territory**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nIndia\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Settlement currency**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nINR\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 1. Appointment\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nContoso Industrial appoints Fabrikam Service Partners as an authorised service partner for the territory named above, to carry out warranty repairs on Contoso Industrial equipment and to submit claims in accordance with the Global Warranty Policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 2. Claim submission\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nA claim is submitted within 30 days of the date of repair, giving the part number actually fitted and attaching the inspection report where one was raised. Contoso Industrial adjudicates the claim from the claim-system record, taking running hours from the latest reading held at or before the date of repair. An inspection report matters where an exclusion depends on it; a missing report does not of itself hold a claim.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 3. Labour\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nLabour is reimbursed at the flat-rate allowance published for the operation code, at the regional labour rate in force on the date of repair, in accordance with clause 4.1 of the Global Warranty Policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 6. Parts and handling\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nParts are reimbursed at the published list price for the territory, for the part actually fitted.  \\\\r\\\\nNo handling uplift is payable under this agreement. Parts are reimbursed at list price without addition.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 9. Term\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis agreement runs for three years from execution and renews annually unless either party gives ninety days\\\\u0027 written notice.\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.82521135}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/04-PartnerAgreements/SPA-2024-NWD-IN Northwind Field Services.docx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022SPA-2024-NWD-IN Northwind Field Services\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022python-docx;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022SPA-2024-NWD-IN Northwind Field Services.docx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/04-PartnerAgreements/SPA-2024-NWD-IN Northwind Field Services.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Service Partner Agreement  \\\\r\\\\n_Northwind Field Services \\\\u2014 SPA-2024-NWD-IN_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Agreement reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nSPA-2024-NWD-IN\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Partner**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nNorthwind Field Services\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Partner code**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nD-IN-02\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Territory**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nIndia\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Settlement currency**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nINR\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 1. Appointment\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nContoso Industrial appoints Northwind Field Services as an authorised service partner for the territory named above, to carry out warranty repairs on Contoso Industrial equipment and to submit claims in accordance with the Global Warranty Policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 2. Claim submission\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nA claim is submitted within 30 days of the date of repair, giving the part number actually fitted and attaching the inspection report where one was raised. Contoso Industrial adjudicates the claim from the claim-system record, taking running hours from the latest reading held at or before the date of repair. An inspection report matters where an exclusion depends on it; a missing report does not of itself hold a claim.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 3. Labour\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nLabour is reimbursed at the flat-rate allowance published for the operation code, at the regional labour rate in force on the date of repair, in accordance with clause 4.1 of the Global Warranty Policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 6. Parts and handling\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nParts are reimbursed at the published list price for the territory, for the part actually fitted.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 6.2 Handling uplift\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\n**A handling uplift of 5.0% of the reimbursed parts value is payable to Northwind Field Services in addition to the parts value. The uplift is calculated on parts only and does not apply to labour.**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 9. Term\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis agreement runs for three years from execution and renews annually unless either party gives ninety days\\\\u0027 written notice.\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.82417536}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/04-PartnerAgreements/SPA-2022-TWD-EM Tailwind Equipment Services.docx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022SPA-2022-TWD-EM Tailwind Equipment Services\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022python-docx;Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022SPA-2022-TWD-EM Tailwind Equipment Services.docx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/04-PartnerAgreements/SPA-2022-TWD-EM Tailwind Equipment Services.docx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022  \\\\r\\\\n**\\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#606060\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECONTOSO INDUSTRIAL\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E**\\\\r\\\\n# Service Partner Agreement  \\\\r\\\\n_Tailwind Equipment Services \\\\u2014 SPA-2022-TWD-EM_\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Agreement reference**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nSPA-2022-TWD-EM\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Partner**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nTailwind Equipment Services\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Partner code**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nD-EM-01\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Territory**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nEMEA\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Settlement currency**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nEUR\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 1. Appointment\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nContoso Industrial appoints Tailwind Equipment Services as an authorised service partner for the territory named above, to carry out warranty repairs on Contoso Industrial equipment and to submit claims in accordance with the Global Warranty Policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 2. Claim submission\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nA claim is submitted within 45 days of the date of repair, giving the part number actually fitted and attaching the inspection report where one was raised. Contoso Industrial adjudicates the claim from the claim-system record, taking running hours from the latest reading held at or before the date of repair. An inspection report matters where an exclusion depends on it; a missing report does not of itself hold a claim.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 3. Labour\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nLabour is reimbursed at the flat-rate allowance published for the operation code, at the regional labour rate in force on the date of repair, in accordance with clause 4.1 of the Global Warranty Policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 6. Parts and handling\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nParts are reimbursed at the published list price for the territory, for the part actually fitted.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n### 6.2 Handling uplift\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\n**A handling uplift of 2.5% of the reimbursed parts value is payable to Tailwind Equipment Services in addition to the parts value. The uplift is calculated on parts only and does not apply to labour.**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## 9. Term\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nThis agreement runs for three years from execution and renews annually unless either party gives ninety days\\\\u0027 written notice.\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.81761307}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/05-Reviews/FY26-Q3-Warranty-Review.pptx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022FY26-Q3-Warranty-Review\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022FY26-Q3-Warranty-Review.pptx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/05-Reviews/FY26-Q3-Warranty-Review.pptx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\u003Cslide_1\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003EWarranty Review \\\\u2014 FY26 Q3\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nContoso Industrial \\\\u00B7 Warranty Operations \\\\u00B7 published 16 April 2026\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/slide_1\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cslide_2\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003EHeadlines\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n- Warranty cost at 3.4% of revenue, up 0.6 points \\\\u2014 driven by bulletin activity\\\\r\\\\n- TSB-C-0051 extended 4000-series hydraulic and compressor coverage in January\\\\r\\\\n- TSB-P-0112 superseded TSB-P-0107 in February, narrowing the covered range\\\\r\\\\n- FY26 labour rates took effect 1 April 2026\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/slide_2\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cslide_3\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECoverage position by instrument\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctable\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Instrument**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Applies to**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Period**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cth\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Notes**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/th\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nPOL-WAR-4.2\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nAll, unless varied\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 mo / 6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nGlobal baseline\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nADD-IN-2.1\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nIndia installations\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n18 mo / 5,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nShorter than global\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nADD-EM-1.3\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nEMEA installations\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n24 mo / 6,000 h\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\