E  \\\\r\\\\nCIE-2200-AC-00400 to CIE-2200-AC-00750 inclusive\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Supersedes**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nTSB-P-0107\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\n**Status**\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Ctd\\\\u003E  \\\\r\\\\nCurrent\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/td\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/tr\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/table\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Purpose\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nElevated failure rates have been observed on the valve plate of affected units. Coverage is extended as set out below.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Effect on warranty\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nFor assets within the serial range named above, coverage of the valve plate is extended to 30 months from the date of commissioning, or 7,000 running hours, whichever occurs first.  \\\\r\\\\nThis bulletin names a serial range and therefore takes precedence over the regional addendum and the Global Warranty Policy, in accordance with clause 1.4 of that policy.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## Claim handling\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nClaims adjudicated under this bulletin are recorded against funding code TSB with the reference TSB-P-0112.\\u0022,\\u0022RelevanceScore\\u0022:0.72481084}]},{\\u0022WebUrl\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/05-Reviews/FY26-Q2-Warranty-Review.pptx\\u0022,\\u0022ResourceMetadata\\u0022:{\\u0022Title\\u0022:\\u0022FY26-Q2-Warranty-Review\\u0022,\\u0022Author\\u0022:\\u0022Srikantan Sankaran\\u0022,\\u0022Filename\\u0022:\\u0022FY26-Q2-Warranty-Review.pptx\\u0022,\\u0022URL\\u0022:\\u0022https://microsoftapc.sharepoint.com/teams/ContosoFieldService/Warranty Operations/05-Reviews/FY26-Q2-Warranty-Review.pptx\\u0022},\\u0022Extracts\\u0022:[{\\u0022Text\\u0022:\\u0022\\\\u003Cslide_1\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003EWarranty Review \\\\u2014 FY26 Q2\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n  \\\\r\\\\nContoso Industrial \\\\u00B7 Warranty Operations \\\\u00B7 published 14 October 2025\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/slide_1\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cslide_2\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003EHeadlines\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n- Warranty cost at 2.8% of revenue, down 0.3 points on FY25 Q4\\\\r\\\\n- Claim volume up 11% year on year, driven by the 4000-series installed base\\\\r\\\\n- Average settlement time 8.4 working days against a 10-day target\\\\r\\\\n- India remains the largest region by claim volume\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/slide_2\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cslide_3\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003ECoverage at a glance\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n- Standard coverage: 24 months from commissioning, or 6,000 running hours\\\\r\\\\n- Applies across all product families and all regions\\\\r\\\\n- Labour reimbursed at flat-rate allowance\\\\r\\\\n- Parts reimbursed at territory list price\\\\r\\\\n- Goodwill available at manager discretion for near-miss cases\\\\r\\\\n- TRAP 6. This slide is the stale summary. \\\\u0027Applies across all product families and all regions\\\\u0027 was never true of India (18 months under ADD-IN-2.1) and is wrong for any asset covered by TSB-C-0051 or TSB-P-0112. \\\\u0027Goodwill at manager discretion\\\\u0027 contradicts policy 7.1, which requires recorded authority at tier. A model that trusts this deck over the policy fails the Evidence grounding rubric.\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003C/slide_3\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cslide_4\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n## \\\\u003Cspan style=\\\\u0022color:#1F4E79\\\\u0022\\\\u003EWarranty cost by product family (INR lakh)\\\\u003C/span\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Cchart\\\\u003E\\\\r\\\\n\\\\u003Csour